.th EV I 10/1/77
.sh NAME
ev \*- expression evaluator
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd ev
[expression]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Ev
will evaluate expressions in integer and real arithmetic.
Evaluation is according to standard precedence, parenthesised
expressions being evaluated first.
.s3
The expression may be given as an argument.
If no argument is given, the expressions are taken from standard input.
.s3
Operators allowed are:
.lp +15 15
+	unary and binary
.lp +15 15
-	unary and binary
.lp +15 15
*	multiply (`_' in an argument)
.lp +15 15
/	divide
.lp +15 15
^ or !	exponentiation
.i0
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
yes;
hopefully self explanatory.
.sh AUTHOR
Andrew Hume (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
Unbalanced parentheses split the expression into separate sub expressions.
